.TH "CITADEL" "1" "Sep 2026" "AceTeam" "Citadel CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
citadel-module-reservations - Inspect and manually release job-scoped GPU reservations (aceteam#8248/#8249)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcitadel module reservations [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
A GPU reservation (created by 'citadel run --exclusive' or a local_run_exclusive
MCP tool call) durably evicts non-pinned services and restores them when
released. These commands are the manual escape hatch when that release
didn't happen automatically -- the reserving process crashed or was killed,
or a Release call itself keeps failing for one of the evicted services.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for reservations


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug output

.PP
\fB--no-auto-update\fP[=false]
	Disable automatic update checks and installs for this run (or set CITADEL_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable colorized output

.PP
\fB--node-dir\fP=""
	Override the node config directory (citadel.yaml + services/), bypassing $HOME/ConfigDir resolution. Also settable via CITADEL_NODE_DIR. Scope: manifest/services resolution only -- does NOT redirect network state, the module lockfile, or nodevault.

.PP
\fB--runtime\fP=""
	Container runtime for module containers: docker or podman (default: auto-detect)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcitadel-module(1)\fP, \fBcitadel-module-reservations-list(1)\fP, \fBcitadel-module-reservations-release(1)\fP
